sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Remediated v2 reproduction of Runions et al. (2005) leaf venation space colonization, Murray (1926) / Price et al. (2013) vascular scaling, and Katifori & Magnasco (2012) loop nesting. Resolves all five v1 audit findings by adding real pixel segmentation of both specimen photographs, persistent V(s) source tagging with genealogical hop exclusion and planar segment-intersection enforcement, planar dual areole extraction for Katifori loop nesting, explicit multiscale Strahler tree junction measurement, and machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 90.1, reproducibility 93.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py at c89d18d, image/png, 1138697 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34 (sha256 d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34), spec_fingerprint 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9; artifact_sha256: d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=c22c5f4e26f3e2c6...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-18-venation-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs; transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks; does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.913"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

